Title: Let Chromium use ffmpeg's HEVC decoder
Origin: Thorium (other/enable-hevc-ffmpeg-decoding.patch), ported

The media/ half of 12-add-hevc-ffmpeg-decoder-parser.patch. Compiling the
decoder into ffmpeg is not enough: Chromium asks the platform whether HEVC is
supported, and routes HEVC to the platform decoder or to nothing. These four
changes let the software decoder answer instead.

  media/base/supported_types.cc
                          IsDecoderHevcProfileSupported no longer consults
                          PLATFORM_HAS_OPTIONAL_HEVC_DECODE_SUPPORT and the
                          supplemental profile cache -- which is how a build
                          with no hardware decoder ends up reporting no HEVC at
                          all -- and answers yes whenever the ffmpeg video
                          decoders are built, falling back to the old cache
                          lookup when they are not. IsDecoderBuiltInVideoCodec
                          also admits kHEVC alongside kH264, which is what makes
                          it a "built-in" codec for the rest of media/.
  media/ffmpeg/ffmpeg_common.cc
                          GetAllowedVideoDecoders returns "h264,hevc". This list
                          is checked against ffmpeg's own at runtime, so it has
                          to match what patch 12 configured or the decoder stays
                          unreachable.
  media/filters/ffmpeg_video_decoder.cc
                          IsCodecSupported accepts kHEVC, and kHEVC moves out of
                          the NOTREACHED() arm of GetFFmpegVideoDecoderThreadCount
                          into the H.264 arm, so HEVC gets the same
                          pixels-based thread scaling rather than crashing on
                          the first frame.

Two deliberate differences from Thorium's version:

The IsColorSpaceSupported check at the top of IsDecoderHevcProfileSupported is
kept. Thorium removes it and returns a bare true. Every other codec decoded in
software in this file gates on it -- VP9's copy carries the comment "Color
management required for HDR to not look terrible" -- and HEVC is the codec most
likely to show up as HDR. The check passes BT.2020 with PQ (SMPTEST2084) or HLG
(ARIB_STD_B67), so nothing a real HDR stream uses is turned away; it rejects
only color spaces Chromium cannot manage at all, where claiming support means
decoding and then rendering it wrong.

The copyright headers are left as upstream wrote them, here and in every other
patch in this series.
diff --git a/media/base/supported_types.cc b/media/base/supported_types.cc
index 90e3bda..b4c9a88 100644
--- a/media/base/supported_types.cc
+++ b/media/base/supported_types.cc
@@ -229,25 +229,19 @@ bool IsAudioCodecProprietary(AudioCodec codec) {
 #endif  // !BUILDFLAG(USE_PROPRIETARY_CODECS)
 
 bool IsDecoderHevcProfileSupported(const VideoType& type) {
+  // Every other codec decoded in software here gates on the color space, and
+  // HEVC is the one most likely to arrive as HDR. BT.2020 with PQ or HLG passes
+  // this; only a color space Chromium cannot manage at all is rejected.
   if (!IsColorSpaceSupported(type.color_space)) {
     return false;
   }
 
-#if BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_PLATFORM_HEVC)
-#if BUILDFLAG(PLATFORM_HAS_OPTIONAL_HEVC_DECODE_SUPPORT)
-#if BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
-  if (!base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(kPlatformHEVCDecoderSupport)) {
-    return false;
-  }
-#endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
-  return GetSupplementalDecoderVideoProfileCache()->IsProfileSupported(
-      type.profile);
-#else
+#if BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_FFMPEG_VIDEO_DECODERS)
   return true;
-#endif  // BUIDFLAG(PLATFORM_HAS_OPTIONAL_HEVC_DECODE_SUPPORT)
 #else
-  return false;
-#endif  // BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_PLATFORM_HEVC)
+  return GetSupplementalDecoderVideoProfileCache()->IsProfileSupported(
+      type.profile);
+#endif  // BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_FFMPEG_VIDEO_DECODERS)
 }
 
 bool IsDecoderVp9ProfileSupported(const VideoType& type) {
@@ -588,7 +582,7 @@ bool IsEncoderOptionalVideoType(const media::VideoType& type) {
 
 bool IsDecoderBuiltInVideoCodec(VideoCodec codec) {
 #if BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_FFMPEG_VIDEO_DECODERS) && BUILDFLAG(USE_PROPRIETARY_CODECS)
-  if (codec == VideoCodec::kH264) {
+  if (codec == VideoCodec::kH264 || codec == VideoCodec::kHEVC) {
     return true;
   }
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_FFMPEG_VIDEO_DECODERS) &&
diff --git a/media/ffmpeg/ffmpeg_common.cc b/media/ffmpeg/ffmpeg_common.cc
index 280dce6..fe27fd5 100644
--- a/media/ffmpeg/ffmpeg_common.cc
+++ b/media/ffmpeg/ffmpeg_common.cc
@@ -69,7 +69,7 @@ VideoColorSpace GetGuessedColorSpace(const VideoColorSpace& color_space) {
 const char* GetAllowedVideoDecoders() {
   // This should match the configured lists in //third_party/ffmpeg.
 #if BUILDFLAG(USE_PROPRIETARY_CODECS) && BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_FFMPEG_VIDEO_DECODERS)
-  return "h264";
+  return "h264,hevc";
 #else
   return "";
 #endif
diff --git a/media/filters/ffmpeg_video_decoder.cc b/media/filters/ffmpeg_video_decoder.cc
index 3e35153..39786da 100644
--- a/media/filters/ffmpeg_video_decoder.cc
+++ b/media/filters/ffmpeg_video_decoder.cc
@@ -71,19 +71,19 @@ static int GetFFmpegVideoDecoderThreadCount(const VideoDecoderConfig& config) {
   // Only add more threads for those codecs that we know will benefit.
   switch (config.codec()) {
     case VideoCodec::kUnknown:
+      // We do not compile ffmpeg with support for any of these codecs.
+      NOTREACHED();
+
+    case VideoCodec::kH264:
+    case VideoCodec::kHEVC:
     case VideoCodec::kVC1:
     case VideoCodec::kMPEG2:
-    case VideoCodec::kHEVC:
     case VideoCodec::kVP9:
     case VideoCodec::kAV1:
     case VideoCodec::kDolbyVision:
     case VideoCodec::kTheora:
     case VideoCodec::kMPEG4:
     case VideoCodec::kVP8:
-      // We do not compile ffmpeg with support for any of these codecs.
-      NOTREACHED();
-
-    case VideoCodec::kH264:
       // Normalize to three threads for 1080p content, then scale linearly
       // with number of pixels.
       // Examples:
@@ -117,8 +117,9 @@ static void ReleaseVideoBufferImpl(void* opaque, uint8_t* data) {
 
 // static
 bool FFmpegVideoDecoder::IsCodecSupported(VideoCodec codec) {
-  // We only build support for H.264.
-  return codec == VideoCodec::kH264 && IsDecoderBuiltInVideoCodec(codec);
+  // We only build support for H.264 / H.265.
+  return (codec == VideoCodec::kH264 || codec == VideoCodec::kHEVC) &&
+         IsDecoderBuiltInVideoCodec(codec);
 }
 
 FFmpegVideoDecoder::FFmpegVideoDecoder(std::unique_ptr<MediaLog> media_log)
